sequenceDiagram
  actor C as Customer
  participant S as Supervisor
  participant B as BillingAgent
  participant G as ToolGateway
  participant BSS as BSS adapter
  participant K as Knowledge base
  participant H as Human specialist
  C->>S: Explain my bill
  S->>B: handle
  B->>G: billing.explain_charges
  G->>BSS: invoice and line items
  B->>G: usage.get_summary (CDR evidence)
  B->>K: tariff and policy
  B-->>C: Itemised explanation with invoice, CDR and KB references
  C->>S: That roaming charge is wrong
  S->>B: dispute
  B->>G: billing.register_dispute
  G->>G: consent for case processing
  G-->>C: Confirmation required
  C->>S: YES
  G->>BSS: register dispute
  BSS-->>G: dispute reference
  G-->>C: Dispute reference and next step
  Note over B,H: Credits are never autonomous. Any credit is routed for human approval.
  G-->>H: Approval queue item
